A||N||9||3fifty||1.5 Din Stereo||||5||
Z||000000||3fifty||02-26-2001||02:53 AM||||I found a nice 1.5 Din cd player at Walmart. It looks like it the same size as the large factory stereo. Does anyone know if a 1.5 din<BR>unit will fill up the large factory hole with<BR>no installation kit?<P>Thanks,<P>3fifty one day!!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||02-26-2001||07:31 AM||||The Fiero radio is 1.5 DIN.  You should not need an adaptor if the new radio has the bolt on brackets for the side of the chassis.<P>I installed a Jensen 1.5 DIN AM/FM/Cassette/CD unit.  It has a removable face plate and front load cassette and CD.  I had to trim the radio surround face plate slightly to allow the radio face plate to be removed.  Can't tell unless I point out where I trimmed.<P>It is a 4 x 40 unit that really livened up the stock speakers in my 85SE (no booming base like the real sound freaks like but much nicer full boodied sound than the original radio produced).<P>I have a double DIN AM/FM/CD/Cassette from a 98 Olds 98 that I'm going to try and stuff into my 85GT.  I'll have to trim the black plastic support piece that lies under the radio and re-work the surround face plate.  If I get it to work I'll post pictures.  This is pretty low on my list though.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||02-26-2001||03:23 PM||||I have a Jenson 1.5 din in my car and it is a POS! It skips horribly on factory CD's and don't even think about trying a CDR in it, it will not even play without skipping while the car is parked. I thought that I may have it mounted wrong, but the one in dad's truck is the same way. Both are identical units from Wal-Mart: AM/FM/CD player that costed about $125||||reg||13
Z||000003||stimpy||02-26-2001||03:33 PM||||Phew, I'm glad I ponied up the extra $100 for my soon-to-be-arriving Pioneer DEH77-DH! I was looking at that Jensen, but didn't like that it only had 1 pair of RCA outputs plus I felt the controls were fussier then the Pioneer. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||02-26-2001||03:46 PM||||The new Pioneer is very nice. I still need to decide if I sell my new Pioneer (in box) or get a GT to install it. Up to now the last one is winning  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||MikeSchaefer||02-26-2001||05:51 PM||||Hi, I have the Jensen 1.5 Din (probably what you saw at walmart), if you have a k's merchandise nearby, they carry them for a little less.  I LOVE the way the jensen looks, but as stated above, it is very skippy but mine plays cd-r's fine.  I have had the pioneers and they sound exactly the same, but you couldn't get the pioneer to skip if you hit it with a bus.  Overall I prefer the jensen better, it looks more like a stock/space age cd player, just pay the money for the model with the nice face (not the all-green model icK) Sorry for the size of these pics, but they give you an idea of how it'll look:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/int4.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/int9.jpg"> <BR>later,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||4
Z||000006||Lisa 86 2m4||02-26-2001||07:03 PM||||I've really been debating on getting the Jensen 715K Model that has AM/FM/CD/Cassette, for a few reasons, it's a 1.5 din with both cd and cassette, looks nice, and at <A HREF="http://www.millionbuy.com" TARGET=_blank>www.millionbuy.com</A>  is only $260. Which sounds like a deal.  This one states it has some kind of new 'antiskip' technology.  Anybody have any input?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||02-26-2001||09:51 PM||||I have a Jensen 715k. The stock Delco radio has a richer sound but I have had no trouble with skipping. My son has one too but if you ever have a low batt. situation it will blow a transister in the turn off circuit in the radio and the face plate light will stay on. If I had it to do over I would look for a different brand. Also there are no seek or scan controls.<p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 02-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||TTiger||02-27-2001||02:01 PM||||You'll be happier with the Pioneer 1.5 din stereo anyway.  I have had two in my Chrysler (first one got ripped off with the rest of my system) and I am going to definately put one into my Fiero when I get to that step with my restoration project.  I never have a problem with skipping or playing CDR's.  There is a lot more potential for a good system with the Pioneer.<P>Just my $.02<BR>Tony  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000009||Oreif||02-27-2001||02:18 PM||||Even with my Fiero lowered and stiffened, I have a very hard time trying to get my Pioneer to skip. Also the Pioneer has more useful features than the Jensen. (Subwoofer control, Radio Station ID, Search, Skip, random play, repeat, Alarm, 2 full ranger RCA's and 1 subwoofer output, CD changer compatable, remote, ETC)||||reg||1
